is it better to start small or think big  and my answer would be  both  i got a great question from one of my  youtube viewers peter who's trying to  start a gym  and he's unsure of if he should start  small rent from other locations and  build up from there or  think big and create his own place from  scratch exactly how he wants it and  continue to launch new businesses from  there and my answer really is to combine  them  so what i would love for you to do  is start small  but then also have that big vision big  picture in mind  here's the reason okay this is real talk  this is important because a lot of  entrepreneurs  think they have to start big  and it's possible and you can you can  have success doing it  the challenge is when you start right  away  big  your chances of failure go up  dramatically because you don't know what  you're doing  you have a concept in your head and  that's great but things are rarely  they rarely work out as you think they  will every time every successful  entrepreneur who's built a business plan  that business plan changes a thousand  times before they end up hitting their  success because the assumptions that you  make are wrong  most of the time  so if you've never done this before if  you've never built a huge business and  you start by going big  you're probably going to make a lot of  mistakes  you're probably going to have some  incorrect assumptions and as a result  your business will fail  and the reason why it's so important is  because if you're investing your life  savings you know if you're mortgaging  your house if you're taking on investors  you can't afford for it to fail  at least i wouldn't if it were my  business if i was taking out a mortgage  or borrowing money from my friends and  family i would want to make darn sure  that that business  had the best shot of success  so i always encourage entrepreneurs to  start small to test  to test your your thoughts to test your  assumptions see if what you think will  work actually works  because you don't know until you  actually get out there and start doing  something  you test small  you show that it works you keep making  improvements you listen to your  customers and keep building up  keep investing back into your business  and then when you have something that  you know works you can raise the money  you need to blow it up  you know if you can get one gym working  really effectively  and that starts from renting from these  other gyms and then building yourself up  if you can get it to the point of one  gym being amazing then you can raise  money to expand you have a formula that  works and it's built on something real  and it dramatically increases the  chances of you being successful  here's a quick example that that can  really relate to what you're doing i'm  an investor in a salsa dancing business  here in toronto  the company is called toronto dance  salsa and how it started was just  renting from gyms  in their off hours so they teach  people how to dance salsa and it'd be  like six to nine at night type of thing  the rent was super cheap  and the founder  didn't have any business experience  before this  she worked in hotels and had  a great corporate life but had never  been an entrepreneur  and so she'd learn the ropes  on a small scale  by building up  classes  from these gyms  and she got to different locations  and she tested her model and she she not  only improved herself as an entrepreneur  learning the skills that you need to be  successful but also learning what it  takes to build a successful salsa  company  how do you teach students what's your  methodology what's the sequence you're  going to teach them in how do you make  sure people come back and stay motivated  although that you can't tell until you  actually go out and start doing it so  she did it on a small scale then  worked with different gyms open up  different locations still renting still  only paying an hourly fee  and she got to the point  where she could expand she had  confidence in the model  and went out and got her own location  in a mall  that cost over a hundred thousand  dollars a year  so instead of paying jim's 40 bucks an  hour she's now spending a hundred  thousand dollars plus per year to have  her location  but it works the business takes off she  teaches five to six thousand students a  year  how to become salsa dancers  but if she went out  took out a huge loan  talked to her family tried to go to  investors to get that hundred thousand  dollars plus just for rent  it wouldn't work there's too many things  that would have gone wrong in the  business all the trial and error  approaches that she took to get that far  wouldn't have been there and she would  have had to shut down and maybe be in  debt for the rest of her life  so start small  test see if it works and keep your big  picture in mind doesn't have to take you  that long to get there  but keep the big picture in mind i don't  want to see you struggling doing this  thing part-time for the rest of your  life  you know at some point you need to see  momentum of progress  and i know it's hard i know  as entrepreneurs we want to see things  happen you know we hate  being down in the details and the  operations and we have big visions and  it's hard to to wait  for things to happen  but it's so important  and it really comes out of me wanting  you to be successful and not having to  be in debt maybe for the rest of your  life and make one of the biggest  regrets of your entire life  by going big too soon  it can happen  but your chances of success go up  dramatically  if you start small and build up  believe  for those of you watching you like the  video  thumbs up below thank you so much and i  want to hear from you please leave a  comment underneath  if you like the video or if you have a  question for your own company i love  hearing from you and i'll make a video  response thank you so much and i'll see  you soon  you
 

